bin/
*.jsonl
bodies/
*.so
*.log
# Root-anchored: an ad-hoc `go build ./cmd/deepai` drops the binary here.
# A bare `deepai` would also match the cmd/deepai/ SOURCE directory at any
# depth, which silently swallowed every new file added under it — git add
# refused them, git status hid them, and the tests still passed locally.
# (`make` builds to bin/, already ignored on line 1.)
/deepai
deepai-debug.log
.deepai/plans/
.superpowers/
.DS_Store
.env
# deepai eval agents: run output is derived data, not source. runs.jsonl is
# large and carries full model output; summary.{md,json} are views over it,
# and with runs.jsonl out of the repo a committed summary is a number nobody
# can trace back to a run. Conclusions worth keeping go in docs/, not here.
# The eval's inputs (eval/agent-cases/) stay tracked and stay pinned: a
# benchmark whose fixtures follow HEAD cannot attribute a delta to a change.
eval/results/
eval/results-recheck-*/
